      "noteEn": "Reverse Polish notation places an operator after its operands. The image similarly puts the Polish sausage to the right of the empty bun—after it in left-to-right reading order—turning the separated hot dog into a postfix-style visual pun. The Spanish caption preserves the wordplay exactly.",
